# This repo: .devcontainer.json runs the prebuilt `dev` image (same volumes as
# docker/dev.sh, so VS Code and a cmux terminal share one Claude login + jj state).
# Build the image first - the devcontainer does not build it:
just docker-build
# then VS Code: "Dev Containers: Reopen in Container"

# `just docker-build` builds THIS CHECKOUT. dev.sh's `build`/`up` do not - they
# hand the GitHub URL to docker and default to main, so while a Dockerfile fix
# is unmerged they give you an image without it (and VS Code then fails with a
# symptom the Dockerfile header blames on the missing fix). Name the branch:
./docker/dev.sh build BRANCH_NAME
# which tree did the image actually come from?
docker run --rm --entrypoint /bin/sh dev -c 'ls -l /lib*/ld-linux-*; env | grep NIX_LD'

# same config from a terminal, no VS Code (npm i -g @devcontainers/cli):
devcontainer up --workspace-folder .
devcontainer exec --workspace-folder . zsh -l

# activation didn't run / tools missing? Dev Containers overrides ENTRYPOINT;
# postStartCommand runs it for you, or by hand inside the container:
/opt/dotfiles/docker/entrypoint.sh true

# container starts but VS Code dies with "Shell server terminated (code: 126)":
# docker exec is broken, not the config - bisect outside VS Code:
docker run -d --name exectest --entrypoint /bin/sh dev -c 'while sleep 1; do :; done' && docker exec exectest echo hi; echo "exit=$?"; docker rm -f exectest

# ANOTHER repo, no image: minimal template - debian + nix feature, tools from
# the dotfiles devShell (no claude; that lives in home-manager, not the shell)
# .devcontainer.json
{
    "image": "debian:bookworm-slim",
    "features": {
        "ghcr.io/devcontainers/features/nix:1": {
            "packages": "",
            "extraNixConfig": "experimental-features = nix-command flakes"
        }
    },
    "postCreateCommand": "nix develop github:alycda/dotfiles -c bash"
}
# "packages" is "" and not []: feature options are typed string/boolean, the
# spec has no array type. The CLI coerces [] to PACKAGES="" so both "work".

# the feature builds an image at Reopen time, and that build can fail two ways
# no config pins away. Both are why THIS repo uses the prebuilt image instead:
#   dies at the END, after "Alright! We're done!", with
#   "error: read of 65536 bytes: Operation not permitted"
#     -> its post-install nix-collect-garbage, EPERM on Docker Desktop for Mac
#     -> docs/solutions/build-errors/devcontainer-nix-feature-gc-eperm.md
#   dies EARLY with "Invalid VERSION value: latest" and an empty valid list
#     -> its unconditional git ls-remote of github.com/NixOS/nix, behind a
#        TLS-inspecting proxy
#     -> docs/solutions/build-errors/devcontainer-nix-feature-version-lookup.md
# both docs carry the Debian+Nix Dockerfile that replaces the feature
